---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import BackToTop from '../components/BackToTop.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const links = {
  googlePrivacy: 'https://policies.google.com/privacy',
  cloudflarePrivacy: 'https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/',
  webAnalytics: 'https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/',
};
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - SecureVault">
  <div class="premium-container" id="main-container">
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <section class="page-header">
        <h1 class="headline">
          Privacy <span class="text-gradient">Policy</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="subheadline">Your vault stays on your phone.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="legal-content hover-section">
        <div class="compliance-box glow-card">
          <div class="compliance-icon">✓</div>
          <div class="compliance-text">
            <h3>Google Play Data safety</h3>
            <p>
              The SecureVault app <strong>collects no data and shares no data</strong>.
              It has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no internet access.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <p>
            Last updated on 20 November 2026. This policy covers the SecureVault
            app for Android and these pages. The rules for using the app are in
            its <a href={`${base}/terms/`}>terms of service</a>.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>No accounts and no servers</li>
            <li>Your vaults stay on your phone, encrypted with your PIN</li>
            <li>No ads, no analytics and no tracking in the app</li>
            <li>No permissions to grant</li>
            <li>Works fully offline</li>
            <li>Visits to these pages counted without cookies</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            SecureVault is published by Chaosmos, the studio Shravan Goswami
            runs. Questions about this policy go to
            <a href="mailto:hello@chaosmos.studio">hello@chaosmos.studio</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>What the app collects</h2>
          <p>
            Nothing. SecureVault has no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no
            crash reporting, and it never asks for your name or email. The app
            has no internet access, so nothing you put in it, and nothing about
            how you use it, can reach us or anyone else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>What the app keeps on your phone</h2>
          <p>Everything stays in the app's private storage on your phone:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Your vaults. Photos, videos, thumbnails, notes, and the names and
              dates of what is in them are encrypted with AES-256 under a key made
              from that vault's PIN.
            </li>
            <li>
              The list of your vaults and their names, protected by your phone's
              Android Keystore.
            </li>
            <li>
              Your settings, and what you write in the disguise itself, such as
              its notes, alarms or mood entries.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            None of this goes into Android's cloud backups or phone-to-phone
            transfers. Uninstalling the app or clearing its storage deletes all
            of it.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you share, open or play a file, the app makes a decrypted copy
            for the other app to use. When you add a photo or video, the photo
            picker hands the app a copy. The app deletes the picker's copy as
            soon as the file is in the vault, and deletes every copy of either
            kind whenever the vault locks and whenever the app starts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>What leaves your phone</h2>
          <p>
            Only what you choose to send: a copy you save to Downloads or share,
            and a backup file you make. A backup file holds a vault's items still
            encrypted, and it opens only with that vault's PIN, so keep it as
            carefully as the vault itself.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Permissions</h2>
          <p>
            SecureVault asks you for no permissions. Photos and videos come in
            through Android's own photo picker, the camera opens through your
            phone's camera app, and copies and backups go to Downloads or through
            the share sheet. The video player adds the network state and wake lock
            permissions, which Android grants without asking. The app has no
            internet permission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Google Play</h2>
          <p>
            The app comes through Google Play. Google may collect data about
            installs, devices and app crashes as part of running the store, under
            <a href={links.googlePrivacy}>Google's privacy policy</a>. That
            happens outside the app, and we see only totals, such as install
            counts, in the Play Console.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>These pages</h2>
          <p>
            These pages are part of the Chaosmos website and are served by
            Cloudflare. Cloudflare handles standard technical data, such as IP
            addresses, to deliver the pages and keep them secure, as described in
            <a href={links.cloudflarePrivacy}>Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Only these pages have analytics, never the app.
            <a href={links.webAnalytics}>Cloudflare Web Analytics</a> counts visits
            to them and how fast each page loads. It records the page, the site
            that sent you, and your country, browser, operating system and device
            type. It sets no cookie, stores nothing on your device and collects no
            personal data, and it does not use your IP address or browser to tell
            visitors apart. We use it only to count visits and to see how fast
            pages load. The pages set no cookies, and your theme choice is kept in
            your browser's local storage.
          </p>
          <p>
            The blog and the help center have an optional comment box powered by
            Giscus, which stores comments as GitHub Discussions in a public
            repository. Commenting needs you to sign in with GitHub, and anything
            you post is public and covered by GitHub's terms and privacy
            statement. If you email us, we use your message and address only to
            reply.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>
            SecureVault is not directed at children under 13, and we do not
            collect personal information from anyone, including children.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            If a future version changes what the app does with data, this page
            will be updated before that version is released, and the date at the
            top will change.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="text-block">
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Email <a href="mailto:hello@chaosmos.studio">hello@chaosmos.studio</a>
            with any question about privacy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <BackToTop />
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const wrapper = document.getElementById('main-container');
  if (wrapper) {
    wrapper.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {
      const rect = wrapper.getBoundingClientRect();
      const x = e.clientX - rect.left;
      const y = e.clientY - rect.top;
      wrapper.style.setProperty('--mouse-x', `${x}px`);
      wrapper.style.setProperty('--mouse-y', `${y}px`);

      const box = document.querySelector('.glow-card');
      if (box) {
        const cardRect = box.getBoundingClientRect();
        const cardX = e.clientX - cardRect.left;
        const cardY = e.clientY - cardRect.top;
        (box as HTMLElement).style.setProperty('--card-x', `${cardX}px`);
        (box as HTMLElement).style.setProperty('--card-y', `${cardY}px`);
      }
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  main {
    padding: 6rem 5% 4rem;
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    z-index: 2;
    position: relative;
  }

  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  .headline {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .subheadline {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .legal-content {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
  }

  .compliance-box {
    background: rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.08);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .compliance-box h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .compliance-box p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .compliance-icon {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 50%;
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .text-block {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  p,
  li {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  strong {
    color: var(--text-main);
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
